So: we have a fair number of the major mythologies represented in
Nethack: Arthurian, Chinese, Egyptian, Greek, Japanese, Norse, Tolkien,
and a few others as well, which Boudewijn Wayers has recently listed on
the net. I thought I'd rectify some major omissions (Indian, 60s) with
two new classes. Some ideas from other posts have been incorporated,
apologies to possessive authors!

For Indian mythology, here is the new Y class: the Yogi.

Gods: Siva (chaotic), Brahma (neutral), Vishnu (lawful). Player can be
any class.

Starting equipment: a +2 staff (magic protection when wielded), some
food rations, a loin cloth (like the shirt, 0 AC unless enchanted), a
blessed ring of levitation (whoever heard of a Yogi who couldn't fly?)

Starting intrinsics: stealth, tell blessed/cursed like priest, sleep
resistance. Low Str/Cha, medium Dex/Con, high Int/Wis.

New function called #meditate or #trance: you are asked how many turns
you wish to meditate. During that time you regenerate HP and magical
energy and decrease your prayer timeout at a very high rate, and don't
get hungry at all. But if a monster comes by while you're in trance,
you could be done for, so it's a gamble. Trances on an altar work like
#offer: you may eventually be given something by your god. (Length of
trance works like weight of corpse in counting the value of the offer.)
Convert the altar first: gods take a dim view of your trancing with the
opposition.

Quest leader: Narada, musician to the gods. Quest nemesis: Ravana, a
titan, surrounded by Hs of various kinds.

Quest item: a magic flute called the flute of Krishna. I'm not sure if
the nemesis uses the stolen artifact against you, but since you have
sleep resistance as starting intrinsic you should be OK. When #invoked
it lets you hurl the Vishnuchakra, a projectile weapon with a wand of
death function. While carried, reduces chance of getting an item cursed
by wizard/minion.

When you become Envoy/Hand/Glory, your god opens your third eye for
you. Besides clairvoyance, this gives you a #gaze function that level
drains your opponent, using up magic and food points. In return, "You
take a vow of celibacy and vegetarianism." Henceforth, eating corpses
or doing it with succubi annoys your god as much as cannibalism who
will reward you with a major loss of alignment, and loss of the #gaze.

Exp level names: 1 Brahmachari, 2 Brahmin, 3 Pujari, 4-6 Sadhu, 7-13
Muni, 14-17 Rishi, 18-20 Maharishi, 21-24 Devarishi, 25-30 Brahmarishi.
Pujari becomes Pujarin and Sadhu becomes Sadhvi if female.

(If you're interested, these translate roughly as: acolyte, initiate,
performer of rituals, ascetic, monk, and various levels of sage.)

...and for 60s mythology here's the F class: the Flowerchild.

Exp level names: 1 Teenybopper, 2 Bobbysoxer, 3 Moptop, 4-6 Teddy
boy/girl, 7-13 Pot smoker, 14-17 Hippie, 18-20 Protester, 21-24
Anti-war activist, 25-30 Anarchist.

Gods: Jimi Hendrix (chaotic), Jim Morrison (neutral), Janis Joplin
(lawful). If your favourite 60s rocker isn't on the list, it may be
because you have to be dead to qualify. Player is chaotic. (Has to be,
because she believes property is theft, and so needs to be able to rip
off stores without annoying god.)

Starting equipment: a tie-dye shirt (0 AC unless enchanted, but may
confuse/blind/stun your opponent if worn outside), some booze, PoHallu,
a musical instrument, some scrolls of taming, some poisoned darts.

Starting intrinsics: fire resistance (i.e you're pretty cool to begin
with), aggravate soldiers and Kops, high likelihood of good sex,
stealth. Low Str/Int, medium Cha/Wis, high Con/Dex.

Here's the deal: you gain brownie points (_hash_ brownie points, heh heh)
with your god when you hallucinate. Max out HP and magical energy
and reset prayer clock instantly, get hungry slower. Surefire gain level
if you have sex while Hallu.

Quest Leader: Jerry Garcia, surrounded by hordes of the Grateful
Undead. Quest Nemesis: Richard Nixon, a &, supported by soldiers and
Kops. So don't forget to pack a towel.

Quest item: blessed luckstone called the Everybody Must Get Stone (cf.
Dylan's Rainy Day Women.) Protects against drain level. When #invoked,
gives you a stoning attack for one round (i.e "Your hands begin to glow
an unearthly yellow" and for the next turn, your weapon acts like a
cockatrice corpse.)

What say, people? devteam? Any other new classes to fill in missing
mythologies?
